\section{Approaches Tried}
We tried multiple combinations of feature extraction and classification. The dataset was first preprocessed (resizing, grayscale conversion), and features were extracted using:

\subsection{HOG + SVM}
HOG computes gradient orientation histograms per cell. The features are concatenated and used to train an SVM.

\begin{itemize}
\item Resize images to $64 \times 64$
\item Use `skimage.feature.hog()` with specified parameters
\item Train a linear SVM using `sklearn.svm.SVC`
\end{itemize}

\subsection{LBP + SVM}
LBP encodes local texture. A histogram of the binary patterns is used as the feature vector.

\begin{itemize}
\item Convert image to grayscale
\item Extract LBP with radius = 3, points = 24
\item Compute histogram and normalize
\item Train a linear SVM
\end{itemize}

\subsection{HOG/LBP + PCA + SVM}
PCA was used to reduce feature dimensionality before classification:
\begin{itemize}
\item Applied `sklearn.decomposition.PCA` with $n_{components}=100$
\item Transformed training and test data
\item Trained SVM on the reduced feature set
\end{itemize}

\section{Experiments and Results}
We split the dataset into 80\% training and 20\% testing.

\subsection{Evaluation Metrics}
We used accuracy and classification reports (precision, recall, F1-score).

\subsection{HOG + SVM Results}
\begin{itemize}
\item Accuracy: 75.4\%
\item Precision: 76.1\%
\item Observed confusion between categories with similar outlines.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{LBP + SVM Results}
\begin{itemize}
\item Accuracy: 64.2\%
\item Precision: 65.0\%
\item LBP was sensitive to noise in sketches.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{HOG + PCA + SVM Results}
\begin{itemize}
\item Accuracy: 71.8\%
\item PCA reduced feature dimensionality while maintaining performance.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{LBP + PCA + SVM Results}
\begin{itemize}
\item Accuracy: 60.1\%
\item Performance dropped slightly due to information loss in PCA.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Discussion}
\begin{itemize}
\item HOG features outperformed LBP for abstract sketches.
\item PCA helped reduce overfitting and training time.
\item Further improvements could involve CNN-based methods.
\end{itemize}

\section{Summary}
We explored various feature extraction techniques combined with SVM for sketch recognition. HOG+SVM achieved the highest accuracy. While PCA reduced feature size, it did not always improve accuracy. LBP was less robust to the abstract nature of sketches. Future work can explore deep learning-based approaches and ensemble models.

